    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks. Just to be 100% sure on the risk transfer... if the goods are damaged during transit while on the open ocean, who is technically responsible for filing the insurance claim, the seller or the buyer? And does the seller have to provide the buyer with the actual insurance policy document?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While the seller must arrange and pay for insurance under CIF, the risk transfers to the buyer once the goods are on board the vessel. Therefore, even if damage occurs, the buyer is technically responsible for filing the insurance claim with the carrier or insurer. The seller must, however, provide proof of the insurance coverage to the buyer, although they are not strictly required to hand over the actual policy document.",
      "source": "target",
